## 5. Demuxer & Pipeline Integration

In a streaming consumer decoding DJI v13/v14 `.txt` logs:

```
[RawRecordEnvelope] 
      │
      ▼
Check is_plaintext_bypass() || get_feature_point(version, type) == 8
  ├── YES ──► Immediate Plaintext (KeyStorage 56, FlightRecordRecover 50)
  │
  └── NO  ──► 1. xor::descramble_slice(&payload[1..], &mut ct_buf, key)
              2. aes_engine.decrypt_into(feature_point, ciphertext, &mut pt_buf)
              3. TelemetryDecoder::parse(plaintext)
```

### Clean Memory & Zero Allocations
All buffers (`ct_buf`, `pt_buf`, `out_buf`) can reside on the stack or in pre-allocated scratch arenas, achieving **0 heap allocations per telemetry frame** throughout the decryption pipeline.

